WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:02.367
-It's always great to see you.

00:00:02.367 --> 00:00:03.968
But I told you we were
going to get that win, right?

00:00:03.968 --> 00:00:05.467
-I feel so, like...
-Yes, you -- We did it.

00:00:05.467 --> 00:00:06.634
We got it.
-...invincible.

00:00:06.634 --> 00:00:09.200
-Yes! Come on! We crushed it!
-Invincible.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:10.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.934 --> 00:00:12.234
-I knew we would be
good together.

00:00:12.234 --> 00:00:13.934
Thanks for coming back
to the show.

00:00:13.934 --> 00:00:16.300
You know, there's a big debate
always around this time.

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:18.934
Is it too early to get ready
for Christmas?

00:00:18.934 --> 00:00:21.000
Can you listen to the music?
Can you decorate?

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.267
And you say --

00:00:22.267 --> 00:00:25.968
-I say it's not too early to
start on Halloween.

00:00:25.968 --> 00:00:28.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:30.200
-But, I mean, is that when
you start, around Halloween?

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:31.667
No.
-Well, I pull the tree out.

00:00:31.667 --> 00:00:36.133
And, I mean, it's --
Mine is out.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:38.434
I haven't decorated it.
I'm doing that when I get back.

00:00:38.434 --> 00:00:40.367
-Oh, yeah.
So, the -- But the tree is out.

00:00:40.367 --> 00:00:41.567
Is it -- is it plugged --

00:00:41.567 --> 00:00:45.300
-It's lit and plugged in,
but no decorations, guys.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.767
-Yeah. Now, do you do --
Do you do a real tree?

00:00:47.767 --> 00:00:49.067
-No, no, no.
-Fake tree.

00:00:49.067 --> 00:00:51.033
-I like the fake tree
because you have

00:00:51.033 --> 00:00:52.934
the lights evenly distributed.

00:00:52.934 --> 00:00:54.767
-Wow!

00:00:54.767 --> 00:00:57.634
-Otherwise, you'll have pockets,
you know, that are just...

00:00:57.634 --> 00:00:59.634
-Do you have the whole family --
Do you have every --

00:00:59.634 --> 00:01:02.400
Do you host everyone
for the holidays?

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.534
-No.

00:01:04.534 --> 00:01:07.501
I usually go home
because it's easier for me,

00:01:07.501 --> 00:01:10.834
but -- and, in all honesty,
nobody in my life

00:01:10.834 --> 00:01:13.968
would ever want me
to host a party or...

00:01:13.968 --> 00:01:15.534
-I think you would be
a great host.

00:01:15.534 --> 00:01:18.000
-Well, only because --
And I just want to see

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.501
if you guys agree
and if you agree.

00:01:20.501 --> 00:01:22.634
I have -- I tap out early.

00:01:22.634 --> 00:01:26.467
So I'm ready to be done before
other people are,

00:01:26.467 --> 00:01:27.567
and if --

00:01:27.567 --> 00:01:28.634
-No, no, no, no, no.

00:01:28.634 --> 00:01:30.667
-If you're hosting,
you can't go,

00:01:30.667 --> 00:01:32.834
"Ooh, guys, you know,
dinner is from 8:00 to 10:00.

00:01:32.834 --> 00:01:35.767
It's 9:30."

00:01:35.767 --> 00:01:37.133
-You've got to go to
10:00 at least.

00:01:37.133 --> 00:01:38.901
-Yes.

00:01:38.901 --> 00:01:41.000
I just -- So --
-Wow.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.400
-Yeah.
-No, yeah. Then you can't.

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:46.100
But have you ever tried it?

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:49.801
-"Dinner is from 8:00 to 10:00.
It's 9:30."

00:01:49.801 --> 00:01:51.434
I am going to try next year.

00:01:51.434 --> 00:01:52.501
-Yeah. Oh, you will?
-I am. Yeah.

00:01:52.501 --> 00:01:53.801
-Okay, good.
-Yeah.

00:01:53.801 --> 00:01:55.467
-So then, after next year,
I want you to come back

00:01:55.467 --> 00:01:57.200
on the show to discuss
how it went.

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:00.434
-I can tell you,
I'm going to be really panicked.

00:02:00.434 --> 00:02:02.200
-Around 9:30, how do we get
the family up politely?

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:04.367
-How do we get them out?
How do we get them out? Yeah.

00:02:04.367 --> 00:02:05.501
-I want to talk to you
about this,

00:02:05.501 --> 00:02:07.968
because you told me
a very funny story,

00:02:07.968 --> 00:02:10.133
and you brought a photo,
as well.

00:02:10.133 --> 00:02:13.033
It's Halloween,
and you were getting some candy.

00:02:13.033 --> 00:02:14.868
-Yeah.
-Getting ready for Halloween.

00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:17.000
And -- Well, do we --

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:20.901
-Well, so, here's the thing.
I never have cash with me.

00:02:20.901 --> 00:02:22.067
And I was all excited.

00:02:22.067 --> 00:02:24.300
I'm also that customer
who's, like, ready.

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:26.400
I don't want to be fumbling for
my cash or my credit card

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:27.534
when I'm at the register.

00:02:27.534 --> 00:02:29.267
-Me neither.
-So I like to find it.

00:02:29.267 --> 00:02:32.067
I'm like, "Do I have cash?"
Like, "Do I have $5?"

00:02:32.067 --> 00:02:34.234
And I found a $100 bill
in my wallet.

00:02:34.234 --> 00:02:35.567
And I was so proud because

00:02:35.567 --> 00:02:37.567
I felt like I had
found a treasure.

00:02:37.567 --> 00:02:41.200
And, so, I'm glad
I'm one of those people

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:42.634
who likes to be prepared,

00:02:42.634 --> 00:02:44.901
because I'm looking at the
$100 bill and I'm like,

00:02:44.901 --> 00:02:47.734
"Ben Franklin looks
really, really weird."

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:49.601
-Yeah.

00:02:49.601 --> 00:02:52.634
And this is the -- This is what
you gave the person at the --

00:02:52.634 --> 00:02:53.801
at the store.

00:02:53.801 --> 00:02:57.734
-I realized...

00:02:57.734 --> 00:03:02.234
I realized it was
a prop from "Spirited"

00:03:02.234 --> 00:03:04.701
and I almost paid with it.

00:03:04.701 --> 00:03:05.701
Can you imagine?

00:03:05.701 --> 00:03:07.434
-Counterfeit
Ryan Reynolds money.

00:03:07.434 --> 00:03:11.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:11.067 --> 00:03:13.234
[ Laughs ]
You almost went to jail.

00:03:13.234 --> 00:03:14.467
-I almost went to jail.

00:03:14.467 --> 00:03:16.567
-You almost went to prison
over Ryan Reynolds.

00:03:16.567 --> 00:03:18.267
How did you end up with this?
What is this?

00:03:18.267 --> 00:03:20.968
-Well, it's a prop from the set,
and I saw it on the floor

00:03:20.968 --> 00:03:23.434
and I thought, "Wow, that's a
great -- It looks real."

00:03:23.434 --> 00:03:25.267
And I thought, because I never
have money in my wallet,

00:03:25.267 --> 00:03:26.601
that I would remember.

00:03:26.601 --> 00:03:29.534
We shot it a year ago.
This just happened Halloween.

00:03:29.534 --> 00:03:30.968
-Yeah.

00:03:32.634 --> 00:03:33.834
That's so funny.

00:03:33.834 --> 00:03:35.801
But now is it out of
your purse and safe?

00:03:35.801 --> 00:03:36.901
-I have it on a shelf.

00:03:36.901 --> 00:03:39.467
I save props and things
from sets.

00:03:39.467 --> 00:03:41.968
So I have it on my bookshelf.

00:03:41.968 --> 00:03:43.634
And I'm never saving money
from any other set.

00:03:43.634 --> 00:03:44.968
-Yeah, there you go.
You learned your lesson.

00:03:44.968 --> 00:03:46.501
-Yeah.
-Let's talk about "Spirited."

00:03:46.501 --> 00:03:48.367
Congratulations on this.
You know, I...

00:03:48.367 --> 00:03:50.067
-Thank you. Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:50.067 --> 00:03:54.501
-It's a big, fun
comedy, holiday musical.

00:03:54.501 --> 00:03:56.634
Can we set up what it's about?
-Yes.

00:03:56.634 --> 00:04:00.634
It's a retelling
of "A Christmas Carol,"

00:04:00.634 --> 00:04:02.133
but it's from
the ghosts' perspective.

00:04:02.133 --> 00:04:03.234
-Which I think is brilliant.
-Yeah.

00:04:03.234 --> 00:04:05.434
-Yeah, so,
Will Ferrell is actually

00:04:05.434 --> 00:04:07.767
looking at his past and going,
"Why am I doing this?

00:04:07.767 --> 00:04:09.734
Why am I finding
a Scrooge every year?

00:04:09.734 --> 00:04:11.000
What's the point of all this?"

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:12.067
Yeah.
-Yes.

00:04:12.067 --> 00:04:13.200
-Last time you were on our show,

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:15.267
you were just about to
start filming.

00:04:15.267 --> 00:04:18.667
and you were very excited but
also a little nervous,

00:04:18.667 --> 00:04:21.200
because the director asked you
if you ice-skate.

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:22.234
-If I ice-skate.

00:04:22.234 --> 00:04:25.534
And I immediately said,
"Uh, no."

00:04:25.534 --> 00:04:29.367
And so they got me
this world-class trainer,

00:04:29.367 --> 00:04:31.667
Elladj Baldé, from Canada.

00:04:31.667 --> 00:04:32.968
And that --

00:04:32.968 --> 00:04:34.467
-I should say this is a photo.

00:04:34.467 --> 00:04:36.567
This is not the trainer,
Elladj Baldé.

00:04:36.567 --> 00:04:40.501
This is you and
a plastic seal for children.

00:04:40.501 --> 00:04:42.067
That is for --

00:04:42.067 --> 00:04:44.601
usually for children
to learn how to ice-skate.

00:04:44.601 --> 00:04:46.601
But this is before you
got the training.

00:04:46.601 --> 00:04:47.868
-Before I got the training.

00:04:47.868 --> 00:04:49.434
-Yeah. And you were nervous.
-I was --

00:04:49.434 --> 00:04:50.767
-But we showed this on the show,

00:04:50.767 --> 00:04:54.267
and I appreciate you being
so, well, confident.

00:04:54.267 --> 00:04:55.400
-But here's the thing.

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:58.734
I realized that
I could master the ice.

00:04:58.734 --> 00:04:59.934
-Yes.
-I did.

00:04:59.934 --> 00:05:02.868
-Conquered your demons.
And we have a clip.

00:05:02.868 --> 00:05:04.767
We'll see how it ended up going.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:05:04.767 --> 00:05:06.601
-Here's Octavia Spencer.
Watch this.

00:05:10.567 --> 00:05:12.701
What? Didn't fall down?

00:05:12.701 --> 00:05:15.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:15.968 --> 00:05:18.934
-I did not fall down.

00:05:18.934 --> 00:05:22.133
I did learn
how to be on the ice.

00:05:22.133 --> 00:05:26.334
-Uh-huh.
-But I called it "ice scooting."

00:05:26.334 --> 00:05:28.767
-Were you --
-I wasn't wearing...

00:05:28.767 --> 00:05:29.868
-Skates.
-...the skates.

00:05:29.868 --> 00:05:31.033
No, I --
-Right there.

00:05:31.033 --> 00:05:33.334
-Yeah. No, I just decided
I could scoot on

00:05:33.334 --> 00:05:36.367
if I had my sneakers.

00:05:36.367 --> 00:05:39.000
-You ice-acted? You skate-acted?

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:40.400
-Well, the director was like,
"Don't do that.

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:41.434
Nobody does that."

00:05:41.434 --> 00:05:42.968
It's like driving
and doing this.

00:05:42.968 --> 00:05:45.167
So I was like, "Oh, I guess I
probably --" Yeah.

00:05:45.167 --> 00:05:47.100
So I didn't.
-But you sing also in this.

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:48.801
This is a lot of pressure for
you to do a lot of stuff.

00:05:48.801 --> 00:05:51.667
-There were a lot of new things,
a lot of moving parts.

00:05:51.667 --> 00:05:52.801
So I --
-Academy Award winner.

00:05:52.801 --> 00:05:54.133
You got to do it all now.
-Yeah.

00:05:54.133 --> 00:05:55.801
-Come on.
They expect it from you.

00:05:55.801 --> 00:05:57.634
-Yeah.
-But you sound phenomenal.

00:05:57.634 --> 00:05:59.901
-Well, thank you, but
it took a lot to get me there,

00:05:59.901 --> 00:06:05.901
because I had no idea
what it takes to do a musical,

00:06:05.901 --> 00:06:07.834
because --
Well, here's the thing.

00:06:07.834 --> 00:06:08.934
We all sing every day.

00:06:08.934 --> 00:06:10.868
I don't consider myself
a singer.

00:06:10.868 --> 00:06:13.200
But I thought I could
probably do it,

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:15.834
because, you know, when you're
singing with the radio,

00:06:15.834 --> 00:06:17.667
you sound so good, right?

00:06:17.667 --> 00:06:18.767
You're like...

00:06:18.767 --> 00:06:20.200
-Yeah, I might
roll down the windows.

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:22.100
I sound pretty good.
I want people to hear this one.

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:23.834
Yeah.
-You know, you hit the notes.

00:06:23.834 --> 00:06:26.334
But you realize that
you're singing very low, like...

00:06:26.334 --> 00:06:27.367
♪ Hello ♪

00:06:27.367 --> 00:06:28.501
-Ooh.
-You know, it's --

00:06:28.501 --> 00:06:30.934
-♪ Is it me
you're looking for? ♪

00:06:30.934 --> 00:06:33.400
-Wow. That was magic.
-It was magic.

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:35.467
And then I realized, you know,
they were going to

00:06:35.467 --> 00:06:37.901
have a microphone, so I thought
I would just use my little --

00:06:37.901 --> 00:06:40.634
my radio singing voice.

00:06:40.634 --> 00:06:43.434
And it's kind of small,
like a little mouse voice.

00:06:43.434 --> 00:06:48.067
And the music --
the voice coach, Eric Vetro,

00:06:48.067 --> 00:06:49.734
was like, "Yeah, I'm going to --

00:06:49.734 --> 00:06:52.133
I'm going to need you to
sing out."

00:06:52.133 --> 00:06:53.167
-Project, yeah.
-Yeah, project.

00:06:53.167 --> 00:06:54.434
-You got to project
a little bit.

00:06:54.434 --> 00:06:56.200
Yeah, this movie is not
a text message,

00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:57.734
so we need to hear you.

00:06:57.734 --> 00:06:59.634
-And I literally
started panicking,

00:06:59.634 --> 00:07:02.767
because I thought, "Well,
what have I signed on to do?"

00:07:02.767 --> 00:07:05.167
I thought I was going to walk
around, you know...

00:07:05.167 --> 00:07:06.501
♪ Singing mouse voice ♪

00:07:06.501 --> 00:07:07.767
-You crushed it.
-Thank you.

00:07:07.767 --> 00:07:09.734
-And you're singing with Will,
with Will Ferrell.

00:07:09.734 --> 00:07:11.000
-Well, then he
makes it easier, though.

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:12.234
-Yeah, he's fun.

00:07:12.234 --> 00:07:14.400
-So, we have a musical director
who taught me

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:19.834
how to use the lyrics
to the song as a monologue.

00:07:19.834 --> 00:07:21.267
Now, that I understand, but...

00:07:21.267 --> 00:07:23.167
♪ Singing in mouse voice ♪

00:07:23.167 --> 00:07:25.634
-No, I think you have it.
You sound so great.

00:07:25.634 --> 00:07:28.067
And it's very funny
and it's very holiday

00:07:28.067 --> 00:07:30.200
and it puts you in a good mood,
in a good spirit.

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:31.968
You do get in
the holiday spirit.

00:07:31.968 --> 00:07:33.033
-You do.
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:07:33.033 --> 00:07:34.968
Here's Octavia Spencer
in "Spirited."

00:07:34.968 --> 00:07:36.200
Take a look.

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:37.767
-Hey!
[ Chuckles ]

00:07:37.767 --> 00:07:42.300
You're back and in
a-a boldly tight suit.

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:44.634
-Yeah, it -- it is
a little snug.

00:07:44.634 --> 00:07:48.801
-No, I-I like it.
It's kind of a Euro fit.

00:07:48.801 --> 00:07:49.934
-Oh.
-And I like it on you.

00:07:49.934 --> 00:07:51.868
-Yeah. Yeah, it is a Euro fit,

00:07:51.868 --> 00:07:54.033
because I buy all my clothes
in Germany.

00:07:54.033 --> 00:07:55.167
-Oh.
-Yeah.

00:07:55.167 --> 00:07:59.467
-I can see.
-Um, uh, sorry.

00:07:59.467 --> 00:08:03.133
But would you -- would you want
to, uh, go somewhere

00:08:03.133 --> 00:08:05.834
and maybe -- I don't -- No.

00:08:05.834 --> 00:08:06.868
-No, I --
-You don't even have to answer.

00:08:06.868 --> 00:08:09.234
-Yeah. I would love to.

00:08:09.234 --> 00:08:10.534
-Oh, great. Really?

00:08:10.534 --> 00:08:12.200
-Totally. I love somewhere.

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:14.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:14.734 --> 00:08:17.033
-"I love somewhere."
-It's my favorite place.

00:08:17.033 --> 00:08:19.467
-Me too. Octavia Spencer.

00:08:19.467 --> 00:08:22.033
"Spirited"
is in theaters this Friday

00:08:22.033 --> 00:08:25.801
and on Apple TV+,
globally, November 18th.

00:08:25.801 --> 00:08:27.734
We'll be right back with
Matthias Schweighoefer.

00:08:27.734 --> 00:08:28.801
Stick around, everybody.

